      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "COPD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " rescue SABA for every pt; albuterol 2 puffs 4 to 6 × a day prn = USU the drug of choice for episodic dyspnea or early exacerbation tx."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "BBs block the effect and can cause severe bronchospasm in asthma (cardioselective only, w caution, if ⍉alt). Loop/thiazide diuretics: hypokalemia and ECG chgs can worsen. Digoxin levels may fall; consider monitoring. MAOIs/TCAs (or w.in 2 wks of stopping): extreme caution, vasc effects potentiated."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Prime (4 sprays away from the face, shaking b4 each) b4 first use, after > 2 wks unused, or if dropped. Needing more doses than usual may mean worsening asthma: seek reeval."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "OD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " excess β stim (seizures, angina, HTN or hypotension, tachy up to 200/min, arrhythmias, tremor, hyperglycemia, hypokalemia, met acidosis); ♡ arrest and death are poss. Tx: stop the drug, Sxtomatic care; a cardioselective BB may be considered judiciously (it can cause bronchospasm)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
